{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"ADR Dangerous Goods Lookup"},"description":"Look up the full European road dangerous-goods (ADR 2025) Table A entry for a substance \u2014 all 20 columns, from class, packing group and labels through special provisions, limited/excepted quantities, packing instructions, tank codes, carriage provisions, transport category, tunnel restriction code and hazard identification number \u2014 and what each of those codes means (resolved_codes). 2,939 entries across all 9 classes, from UNECE ADR 2025. Provide exactly ONE of: un_number (every packing-group variant of it; \"1203\", \"UN1203\" and \"un 1203\" are equivalent; explosives keep their leading zero), search (partial proper shipping name), hazard_class, or un_numbers (batch). A search with no hits errors with the closest names. For an LQ/EQ quantity check use adr_lq_eq_check; for 1.1.3.6 small-load points adr_exemption_calculator; for an identifier of unknown kind resolve_reference. Editions: edition (\"2025\" | \"2027\") and as_of (YYYY-MM-DD) choose the ADR edition \u2014 edition wins, else the date picks it (ADR 2025 before 2027-01-01, ADR 2027 from then; ADR 2025 may still be applied until 2027-06-30). An answer on a named edition carries adr_edition; neither sent, the answer is ADR 2025 until 2027-01-01. edition (\"2025\" | \"2027\") and as_of choose the ADR edition; neither sent, ADR 2025 until 2027-01-01. Rate-limited: a limit error carries reset_at, the UTC time the allowance resets. A factual compilation of the ADR table, not legal or compliance advice; classification remains the consignor's responsibility.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"as_of":{"description":"The date the answer is for, YYYY-MM-DD (default today, UTC).","pattern":"^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$","type":"string"},"editio